<p>Police in London launched an investigation after four ambulances belonging to Hatzola Northwest, a Jewish volunteer emergency medical service, were set on fire in Golders Green early on March 23. The Metropolitan Police said officers were called to Highfield Road at about 1:45 a.m. after reports of a fire and are treating the incident as an antisemitic hate crime. No injuries were reported, but the attack damaged emergency vehicles used by a community response group. The case has drawn attention because the vehicles belonged to a volunteer ambulance organization that provides emergency medical response in north London. Police have not detailed a motive beyond their suspicion of antisemitism, but the focus of the investigation is striking: someone targeted medical service vehicles rather than ordinary private property, raising concern about both community safety and the continuity of volunteer emergency support.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/35FQrT_ZgwXXV0caqsb25y0MtbbQINk3Nc_r2sB_yRm81rdzI2kKUx0lLMFDd5TNKPrgqFXaiA8Hq6LiLFMkc4QAjYFG814-XlaE_wI0IpEUHzHlFLftl9rnughFIY1onJ3K2ynHgs-q-AM5k08XZkdLakLDKO7uwwqB7f9b_A' alt='Emergency vehicles linked to the London arson investigation.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Fire response: The London Fire Brigade said the blaze damaged four Hatzola Northwest ambulances.</li><li>Scene details: The vehicles were parked on Highfield Road in Golders Green, a north London area with a large Jewish community.</li><li>Service role: Hatzola Northwest is a volunteer-led Jewish community ambulance service that provides rapid medical response.</li><li>Casualty update: Across the covered outlets, reports said no casualties were recorded despite the destruction of at least four vehicles.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Metropolitan Police: Police said officers remained at the scene and were treating the arson as an antisemitic hate crime, showing that investigators see bias as central to the case. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/mar/23/jewish-volunteer-ambulances-fire-golders-green-suspected-arson-antisemitic-ntwnfb'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>London Fire Brigade: Fire officials focused on the operational damage, saying the blaze affected four ambulances belonging to Hatzola Northwest. (<a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/hatzola-northwest-jewish-community-ambulances-set-on-fire-in-london-in-antisemitic-attack-amid-iran-war-11252948#publisher=newsstand'>NDTV</a>)</li><li>Hatzola Northwest: Across reports, the organization was described as a volunteer emergency responder for the Jewish community, underscoring that the damaged vehicles support frontline medical aid rather than commercial activity. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/london-jewish-community-ambulances-torched-suspected-hate-crime-police-say'>Reuters via Al-Monitor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/hatzola-northwest-jewish-community-ambulances-set-on-fire-in-london-in-antisemitic-attack-amid-iran-war-11252948#publisher=newsstand'>Jewish Community Ambulances Set On Fire In London In Antisemitic Attack</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/london-jewish-community-ambulances-torched-suspected-hate-crime-police-say'>London Jewish community ambulances torched in suspected hate crime, police say</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/vehicles-belonging-jewish-ambulance-service-set-fire-london-131315454'>Vehicles belonging to Jewish ambulance service set on fire in London in apparent antisemitic attack</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/uk-police-see-antisemitic-motive-in-arson-of-ambulances/a-76479210'>UK police see antisemitic motive in arson of ambulances</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/mar/23/jewish-volunteer-ambulances-fire-golders-green-suspected-arson-antisemitic-ntwnfb'>Arson attack on London vol